+# TotpInput
+
+The `TotpInput` component displays individual input fields for each character of a code. It's designed for entering TOTP codes or recovery codes.
+
+### Basic
+
+The basic usage with 6-digit numeric code.
+
+<Canvas withSource="open">
+    <Story id="components-totpinput--basic" />
+</Canvas>
+
+### Length
+
+The component supports different lengths. This example shows a 4-digit code with an initial value.
+
+<Canvas>
+    <Story id="components-totpinput--length" />
+</Canvas>
+
+### Type
+
+The `type` prop controls whether the input accepts only numbers (`number`) or alphanumeric characters (`alphabet`).
+
+<Canvas>
+    <Story id="components-totpinput--type" />
+</Canvas>
+
+<div class="hidden">
+    <Primary />
+</div>
+
+<ArgsTable story={PRIMARY_STORY} />
